{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01TMgu9Cq7uGnsYq73LACpe9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P2gUFsjpPXPaGsNqiTn6uA","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Explore almanac codebase for architectural friction","subagent_type":"Explore","prompt":"Survey the almanac codebase for architectural friction. This is a bash codebase that implements an \"almanac\" — a toolkit for running autonomous AI agent loops (ralph, harden, converge). The domain model (from CONTEXT.md):\n\n- Loops (ralph/harden/converge) are adapters at `lib/loops/<name>.sh`, dispatched through `lib/loops.sh`\n- Provider adapters (codex/claude) at `lib/providers/<name>.sh`, dispatched via `lib/agent.sh`\n- Run registry + status records in `lib/run.sh`\n- Worker orchestration in `lib/worker.sh`\n- Launcher in `lib/loop-launcher.sh`, hub in `cmd/hub.sh`\n- harden loop in `lib/harden-core.sh`, converge loop in `lib/converge-core.sh`\n\nThe codebase has gone through many convergence rounds already — lots of obvious friction has been removed. I am looking for REMAINING architectural friction. Please:\n\n1. Walk the codebase. Read whole files where useful — `lib/run.sh`, `lib/converge-core.sh`, `lib/harden-core.sh`, `lib/loop-launcher.sh`, `lib/loops.sh`, `cmd/hub.sh`, `lib/agent.sh`, `lib/worker.sh`. Look at `cmd/`, `lib/loops/`, `lib/providers/`.\n\n2. Surface concrete friction with file:line citations. Specifically hunt for:\n   - **Shallow modules**: functions/files whose interface is nearly as complex as their implementation. Pass-throughs that don't earn their keep.\n   - **Untested seams**: places that look like real interfaces but have no test coverage (check `tests/` for what's exercised — `test-*.sh` files).\n   - **Leaky abstractions**: where one module knows the internals of another, or where the same enumeration appears in multiple places (the kind of \"missing seam\" smell).\n   - **Hidden state / global mutation**: env vars or files passed by convention rather than parameter.\n   - **Duplicated logic that should be one helper**: e.g. identical patterns across loop adapters or provider adapters.\n   - **Inconsistencies between loop adapters** — ralph vs harden vs converge — that suggest a missing extraction.\n   - **The Hub & Launcher** — particularly resume/clone logic which has changed often.\n\n3. Apply the deletion test to anything that looks shallow: would deleting it concentrate complexity or just shuffle it?\n\n4. Skip things the repo recently fixed (provider adapters, loop-adapter dispatch via `almanac_loop_adapter_call`, slug helper, run-status record, worker-status record, `agent_capture/stream/raw` split). Don't propose reverting these.\n\nReturn a candidate list, each with: files+lines, problem, deletion-test answer, and one-line proposed direction. Aim for 5-10 candidates ranked by impact. Be ruthless — if there's nothing major left, say so plainly. Keep total response under 1500 words."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1261,"cache_read_input_tokens":44225,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1261},"output_tokens":40,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"274f3ab8-9347-4dfe-9be3-7479874e14e0","uuid":"f72a0ecb-2f1d-459d-a78b-c4188eb3d7ef","request_id":"req_011CbSgs7BM4J4eixfwFDg29"}
